# SKYLIGHT-PHYS: the sky light is captured from the atmosphere in the SAME physical units as the sun (UE
# FSkyLightSceneProxy over the real-time sky capture), and the traced GI reads the sky through that capture, so a
# 100 000 lux sun leaves a readable shade at a sunlight exposure (EV100 15) without a content Min EV.
# Starter: Sun 13376537502658031226, PostProcessVolume 17921165617746467452, Ground albedo 0.55 grey, Cube (0,50,150).
# Reinhard with a far white point so the frame inverts to scene luminance: L = y/(1-y) / exposure, exposure = 1/(1.2*2^EV).
Дано run Scene "Open Scene Starter.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Дано --subject selection set SunElevation 45
Дано set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.AutoExposure false
Дано set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.ManualExposureEV100 15
Дано set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.Tonemapper 1
Дано set 17921165617746467452 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.WhitePoint 1000
Дано set 13376537502658031226 DirectionalLightData.Intensity 100000
Дано run Entity "Cube"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 60
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,350,900
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,-0.35,-1
Тогда-вид 1_lit sunlit ground ~0.55*(E_sun*cos45*T + E_sky)/pi (~10-14k cd/m2); the cube's shadow on the ground 10-25 % of the sunlit ground, not black; the sky blue
# The second scene: the Bistro street under the bistro-sun content (100 000 lux, EV100 14-15) is played by
# Scenarios/Bistro/BISTRO-LOOK.scn (frame 9_day_physical, the open street at -440,300,-230): its shade must read.
